</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ C.2. Feature Extraction Component Ablation ‣ Appendix C Extended Analysis and Experimental Results ‣ AnomaMind: Agentic Time Series Anomaly Detection with Tool-Augmented Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> presents the ablation study of the verification tools. The full AnomaMind framework, equipped with the complete toolset, consistently outperforms variants lacking specific components.
Specifically, excluding <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">local structural feature recognition</span> results in relatively minor performance drops on YAHOO and WSD. This suggests that segment-level and descriptive analyses can partially compensate for the absence of local statistical cues.
However, the removal of <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">global structural feature recognition</span> leads to severe degradation, particularly on IOPS and WSD, where F1 scores drop sharply to 0.125 and 0.277, respectively. This underscores the critical role of structural consistency checks in capturing long-range temporal deviations.
Furthermore, the omission of <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">statistical feature extraction</span> causes a substantial performance decline on the IOPS dataset (with F1 falling to 0.355), highlighting the importance of distributional characterization for accurate verification.
Collectively, these results confirm that the coordinated integration of multi-granular verification tools—spanning point-level detection, segment-level structural analysis, and descriptive statistics—is essential for achieving reliable and accurate anomaly detection across diverse temporal patterns.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>Temperature Sensitivity Analysis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ C.3. Temperature Sensitivity Analysis ‣ Appendix C Extended Analysis and Experimental Results ‣ AnomaMind: Agentic Time Series Anomaly Detection with Tool-Augmented Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> illustrates the sensitivity of our framework to the sampling temperature hyperparameter. Across all datasets, the model exhibits remarkable stability over a broad range of temperature settings, indicating that AnomaMind is not highly sensitive to this parameter.
We observe that moderate temperature values generally yield optimal performance, striking a favorable balance between exploration and deterministic reasoning.
At lower temperatures, the generation process tends to be overly conservative, limiting the diversity of candidate decisions and slightly distinct performance. Conversely, excessively high temperatures introduce stochasticity, resulting in inconsistent anomaly judgments and marginal performance drops.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.13807v1/temp_sensitivity.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/160;" width="476" height="160"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8. </span>Hyperparameter sensitivity analysis regarding sampling temperature on F1 and Best-F1.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1. </span>Data Preprocessing</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Time series data often exhibit significant variations in numerical magnitude and timestamp formats. To ensure accurate anomaly pattern recognition across diverse datasets and enhance model stability, we implement the following preprocessing steps:</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.1. </span>Normalization</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We normalize numerical values to the range <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> via min-max scaling:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}=\frac{x-a}{b-a}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}=\frac{x-a}{b-a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> represent the minimum and maximum values of the time series, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.2. </span>Indexing</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To mitigate the inconsistencies caused by varying timestamp formats and sampling frequencies across datasets, we abstract absolute time into a unified zero-based integer index. Formally, we map the raw time series into an ordered sequence of index-value pairs <math id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\{(t,v_{t})\}_{t=0}^{T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\{(t,v_{t})\}_{t=0}^{T-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> represents the relative temporal step and <math id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sequence length. This standardized representation ensures that the agents focus on relative temporal patterns and output consistent interval coordinates (e.g., <math id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{start},t_{end}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{start},t_{end}]</annotation></semantics></math>) regardless of the original time format.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.3. </span>Detrending</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To mitigate the influence of global trends that are irrelevant to local anomalies, we remove the linear component:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}=x-\hat{x}_{\text{trend}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>trend</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}=x-\hat{x}_{\text{trend}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{\text{trend}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>trend</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{\text{trend}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the linear trend estimated via least squares regression.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2. </span>Sample Construction</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For traditional self-supervised and semi-supervised baselines, we adhere to the TSB-AD benchmark protocol, utilizing the anomaly-free initial segment of the test sequence for training. In contrast, for our proposed method, we incorporate additional distinct sequences from the same dataset as training samples to enhance generalization.
To balance the model’s capacity for processing long-term context with computational efficiency, we set the sample length to 100 and segment the time series using a step size of 100.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3. </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<section id="A4.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.1. </span>F1-Score</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The primary goal of time series anomaly detection is to identify anomalous points while minimizing false alarms. We adopt the standard definitions for Recall, Precision, and F1-score:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recall</span>: Measures the proportion of actual anomalies that are correctly detected. It assesses the model’s ability to capture all relevant instances.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Recall}=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FN}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Recall</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>TP</mi><mrow><mi>TP</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>FN</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Recall}=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FN}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Precision</span>: Quantifies the reliability of the reported anomalies. It indicates the ratio of true anomalies among all positive predictions, reflecting the model’s ability to avoid false alarms.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Precision}=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FP}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Precision</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>TP</mi><mrow><mi>TP</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>FP</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Precision}=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FP}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">F1-score</span>: Provides a balanced metric of overall detection performance. It is calculated as the harmonic mean of Precision and Recall, making it suitable for scenarios with imbalanced data.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{F1-score}=2\times\frac{\text{Precision}\times\text{Recall}}{\text{Precision}+\text{Recall}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>F1-score</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>Precision</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Recall</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>Precision</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>Recall</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{F1-score}=2\times\frac{\text{Precision}\times\text{Recall}}{\text{Precision}+\text{Recall}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For traditional models that output continuous anomaly scores, we apply the widely adopted threshold of <math id="A4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu+3\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu+3\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>; points exceeding this threshold are classified as anomalous. For LLM-based models, points are considered anomalous if they fall within the intervals explicitly generated by the model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.2. </span>Best-F1</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Traditional methods</span>: Best-F1 represents the maximum F1-score obtained by sweeping over possible anomaly score thresholds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Our method</span>: We classify intervals as anomalous only if their associated confidence score meets or exceeds a specific threshold. Consequently, Best-F1 is determined by finding the maximum F1-score across all possible confidence thresholds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Other LLM-based methods</span>: We adhere to the Best-F1 calculation procedures specified in their respective implementations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4. </span>Prompt Templates</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To facilitate reproducibility and provide insight into the underlying reasoning mechanisms of our framework, we present the detailed prompt templates designed for each agentic component. These structured instructions serve as the cognitive blueprint for the system, strictly defining the functional roles, operational constraints, and expected interaction protocols. By standardizing the input-output formats and reasoning pathways, these prompts ensure that the workflow progresses coherently from coarse-grained visual perception to fine-grained evidence analysis.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.SS4.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_tcbfloat"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="901.51" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 901.51" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,901.51) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.57 L 0 893.94 C 0 898.12 3.39 901.51 7.57 901.51 L 469.81 901.51 C 473.99 901.51 477.38 898.12 477.38 893.94 L 477.38 7.57 C 477.38 3.39 473.99 0 469.81 0 L 7.57 0 C 3.39 0 0 3.39 0 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EBF0FF;" fill="#EBF0FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 7.57 L 1.66 871.76 L 475.72 871.76 L 475.72 7.57 C 475.72 4.3 473.07 1.66 469.81 1.66 L 7.57 1.66 C 4.3 1.66 1.66 4.3 1.66 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 873.42 L 1.66 893.94 C 1.66 897.2 4.3 899.85 7.57 899.85 L 469.81 899.85 C 473.07 899.85 475.72 897.2 475.72 893.94 L 475.72 873.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 882.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:23.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.82em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.39)" width="327.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:23.69em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Locator Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 111.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.98em;--ltx-fo-height:53.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.79em;font-size:10pt;" height="838.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 744.59)" width="442.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.98em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Role:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> You are an expert anomaly detection planner. Your objective is to formulate a precise, executable analysis plan by synthesizing visual cues and raw time series data.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input Context:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> You are provided with the following information to guide your planning:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Visual Analysis:</span><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> A description from the Coarse-grained Agent (use as a reference; note that it may flag the entire period or contain false positives).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Data Stream:</span><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The complete time series values and specific </span><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Vision anomaly intervals}</span><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> candidates.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Toolkit:</span><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> A list of </span><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Available Tools}</span><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for execution.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Knowledge:</span><span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Domain-specific constraints and patterns provided in </span><span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Domain Knowledge}</span><span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Planning Guidelines:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Adhere to the following rules when constructing the plan:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I4" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Tool-Centricity:</span><span id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The executing agent is restricted to invoking existing tools. Do not plan complex methods that cannot be directly implemented via the available toolkit.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Specificity:</span><span id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Tailor tool selection to the specific characteristics of the time series. Avoid generic or meaningless steps.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thresholding:</span><span id="A4.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Explicitly set thresholds for tool outputs. Instruct the action agent to disregard fluctuations below these thresholds to reduce false alarms.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Scoping:</span><span id="A4.I4.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Strictly limit the analysis to the accessible intervals provided.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output Protocol:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Structure your response in two strict parts:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I5" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;</span><span id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: An internal reasoning process to deduce the optimal strategy (this will not be executed).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;Plan&gt;</span><span id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The final detailed plan wrapped in tags.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.SS4.tab2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_tcbfloat"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS4.pic2" class="ltx_picture" height="569.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 569.78" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,569.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.57 L 0 562.22 C 0 566.4 3.39 569.78 7.57 569.78 L 469.81 569.78 C 473.99 569.78 477.38 566.4 477.38 562.22 L 477.38 7.57 C 477.38 3.39 473.99 0 469.81 0 L 7.57 0 C 3.39 0 0 3.39 0 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EBF0FF;" fill="#EBF0FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 7.57 L 1.66 540.03 L 475.72 540.03 L 475.72 7.57 C 475.72 4.3 473.07 1.66 469.81 1.66 L 7.57 1.66 C 4.3 1.66 1.66 4.3 1.66 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 541.69 L 1.66 562.22 C 1.66 565.48 4.3 568.12 7.57 568.12 L 469.81 568.12 C 473.07 568.12 475.72 565.48 475.72 562.22 L 475.72 541.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 550.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:23.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.82em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.39)" width="327.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:23.69em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Actor Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 188.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.98em;--ltx-fo-height:24.24em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.39em;font-size:10pt;" height="506.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 335.38)" width="442.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.98em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Role:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> You are a time series anomaly detection expert responsible for tool execution. Your primary function is to translate the high-level analysis plan into concrete tool invocations.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input Context:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I6" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Directive:</span><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The specific </span><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Plan}</span><span id="A4.I6.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> generated by the Planner.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Data:</span><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The </span><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Time Series Values}</span><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> covering the index range </span><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{range}</span><span id="A4.I6.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Execution Protocol:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Adhere to the following strict rules:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I7" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Index Fidelity:</span><span id="A4.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The index values provided are the actual indices from the source CSV. Use these exact values when referencing data points or parameterizing tool calls.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Batch Execution:</span><span id="A4.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Efficiency is paramount. Identify all necessary tools required by the plan and invoke them together in a single turn.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Compliance:</span><span id="A4.I7.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Do not deviate from the plan; focus solely on execution logic.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.SS4.tab3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_tcbfloat"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS4.pic3" class="ltx_picture" height="875.26" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 875.26" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,875.26) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.57 L 0 867.69 C 0 871.87 3.39 875.26 7.57 875.26 L 469.81 875.26 C 473.99 875.26 477.38 871.87 477.38 867.69 L 477.38 7.57 C 477.38 3.39 473.99 0 469.81 0 L 7.57 0 C 3.39 0 0 3.39 0 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EBF0FF;" fill="#EBF0FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 7.57 L 1.66 845.5 L 475.72 845.5 L 475.72 7.57 C 475.72 4.3 473.07 1.66 469.81 1.66 L 7.57 1.66 C 4.3 1.66 1.66 4.3 1.66 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 847.16 L 1.66 867.69 C 1.66 870.95 4.3 873.6 7.57 873.6 L 469.81 873.6 C 473.07 873.6 475.72 870.95 475.72 867.69 L 475.72 847.16 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 856.3)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:23.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.82em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.39)" width="327.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:23.69em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Detector Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 94.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.98em;--ltx-fo-height:53.11em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.59em;font-size:10pt;" height="812.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 734.95)" width="442.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.98em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Role:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> You are the core anomaly detector. Your task is to synthesize tool execution results, the original analysis plan, and raw time series data to render a final, reasoned verdict.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input Context:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I8" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Execution History:</span><span id="A4.I8.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The results from previous tool calls (</span><span id="A4.I8.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Used_Tool_Description}</span><span id="A4.I8.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Strategy:</span><span id="A4.I8.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The original </span><span id="A4.I8.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Plan}</span><span id="A4.I8.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> guiding the analysis.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Knowledge:</span><span id="A4.I8.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Domain-specific rules for fine-grained reasoning (</span><span id="A4.I8.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Domain Knowledge}</span><span id="A4.I8.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response Structure:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Your output must strictly follow this format:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I9" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;think&gt;</span><span id="A4.I9.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: A concise analysis of how the tool results support or refute the anomaly hypothesis.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">JSON Array</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: A list of detected anomalies (or an empty array </span><span id="A4.I9.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[]</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if none). Each object must include:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"interval"</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[start_index, end_index]</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Use actual data indices).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"type"</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The specific name of the anomaly type.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"explanation"</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Concrete reasoning for the decision.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"confidence"</span><span id="A4.I9.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: An integer score from 1 (Low) to 3 (High).</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Critical Constraints:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I10" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Evidence-Based:</span><span id="A4.I10.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Decisions must be grounded in the provided tool results and data values.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Index Fidelity:</span><span id="A4.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Strictly strictly adhere to the original data index values.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.SS4.tab4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_tcbfloat"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS4.pic4" class="ltx_picture" height="989.59" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 989.59" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,989.59) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 7.57 L 0 982.02 C 0 986.2 3.39 989.59 7.57 989.59 L 469.81 989.59 C 473.99 989.59 477.38 986.2 477.38 982.02 L 477.38 7.57 C 477.38 3.39 473.99 0 469.81 0 L 7.57 0 C 3.39 0 0 3.39 0 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EBF0FF;" fill="#EBF0FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 7.57 L 1.66 959.7 L 475.72 959.7 L 475.72 7.57 C 475.72 4.3 473.07 1.66 469.81 1.66 L 7.57 1.66 C 4.3 1.66 1.66 4.3 1.66 7.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#193278;" fill="#193278" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 961.36 L 1.66 982.02 C 1.66 985.28 4.3 987.93 7.57 987.93 L 469.81 987.93 C 473.07 987.93 475.72 985.28 475.72 982.02 L 475.72 961.36 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 970.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:23.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.83em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.53)" width="327.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:23.69em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluator Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.41 283.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.98em;--ltx-fo-height:47.71em;--ltx-fo-depth:19.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="926.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 660.19)" width="442.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.98em;">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Role:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> You are the final reviewer responsible for quality assurance. Your task is to evaluate the detection results for logical consistency and critical errors.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input Context:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I11" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Plan:</span><span id="A4.I11.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The original analysis strategy (</span><span id="A4.I11.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Plan}</span><span id="A4.I11.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I11.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Result:</span><span id="A4.I11.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The detection outcome and reasoning provided by the Detector (</span><span id="A4.I11.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{Detector Result}</span><span id="A4.I11.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Evaluation Criteria:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Adopt a </span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">lenient</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> evaluation stance. Intervention is required </span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">only</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for critical failures.</span></span>
<span id="A4.I12" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pass Condition:</span><span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> If the analysis is generally reasonable, set </span><span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">needs_refinement</span><span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">false</span><span id="A4.I12.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fail Condition:</span><span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Trigger refinement (</span><span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">true</span><span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) </span><span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">only</span><span id="A4.I12.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for major errors (e.g., critical logic flaws, hallucinated data, or complete absence of reasoning).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I12.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I12.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I12.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I12.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rating Scale:</span><span id="A4.I12.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Use "poor" strictly for severe issues. Default to "good" or "acceptable" for minor imperfections.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output Protocol:</span><span id="A4.SS4.pic4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Return a strict JSON object containing the following keys:</span></span>
<span id="A4.I13" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A4.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"issues"</span><span id="A4.I13.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: A list of strings describing critical errors (if any).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"suggestions"</span><span id="A4.I13.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Actionable advice for correction.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"needs_refinement"</span><span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Boolean (</span><span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">true</span><span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">/</span><span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">false</span><span id="A4.I13.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A4.I13.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A4.I13.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"quality_metrics"</span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Ratings for </span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"planning"</span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"tool_usage"</span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"reasoning"</span><span id="A4.I13.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (Value: "good"/"acceptable"/"poor").</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
